@item @kbd{<right>} (@code{vellumory-scroll-right})
@itemx @kbd{<left>} (@code{vellumory-scroll-left})
@kindex <right>
@kindex <left>
@findex vellumory-scroll-right
@findex vellumory-scroll-left
Scroll sideways@comma{} when the page is
  wider than the window.
@item @kbd{M-x vellumory-half-screen-down}
@itemx @kbd{M-x vellumory-half-screen-up}
@findex vellumory-half-screen-down
@findex vellumory-half-screen-up
Scroll by half a screen.  Evil binds
  these to @code{C-d} and @code{C-u}.
@item @kbd{M-x vellumory-scroll}
@findex vellumory-scroll
Scroll by a number of pixels you type.
@end table

Scrolling by a screen is animated: the view glides there in about a
tenth of a second.  @code{vellumory-smooth-scroll} turns this off@comma{} and
@code{vellumory-smooth-scroll-duration} sets the time.  Keyboard macros never
animate.

@cindex numeric prefix
Digits give a count@comma{} as elsewhere in Emacs: @code{5 j} scrolls five steps.  Two
digits are taken by commands of their own (@code{0} fits the page to the window@comma{}
@code{2} shows two pages)@comma{} so for counts that begin with them use @code{C-u}@comma{} as in @code{C-u 20 j}.

