Fit the whole page into the window.
@item @kbd{c} (@code{vellumory-fit-content-width})
@kindex c
@findex vellumory-fit-content-width
Fit the page's content@comma{} without
  its white margins@comma{} to the window's width.
@end table

The zoom in the header line is relative to the window: 100% means the page
fills the window's width.  Each zoom step is 15%@comma{} from 10% to 800%.  The
zoom is part of the place Vellumory remembers for each document.

@cindex margins, cropping
@cindex content width
@code{c} is for papers with wide margins.  Vellumory looks at a small rendering
of the page in view@comma{} finds where the ink is (ignoring specks of dust and
coloured paper)@comma{} and zooms so that the ink fills the window@comma{} with
@code{vellumory-content-padding} pixels of paper on each side.  The fit stays as
the window changes size@comma{} until you zoom some other way.  It works with
single pages only; with two pages side by side@comma{} one horizontal scroll
cannot crop both.  The top and bottom margins stay@comma{} because the pages are
continuous.

@cindex EPUB text size
@cindex text scale

@table @asis
@item @kbd{C-x C-+} (@code{vellumory-text-scale-adjust})
@itemx @kbd{C-x C--}
@itemx @kbd{C-x C-0}
@kindex C-x C-+
@kindex C-x C--
@kindex C-x C-0
@findex vellumory-text-scale-adjust
In EPUB and FB2 books@comma{} make the text larger@comma{} smaller or
  back to @code{vellumory-reflow-text-size}; the book is laid out again and you
  stay at the same point in it.  In other documents these keys zoom in@comma{}
  zoom out or fit the width.
@end table

@node Two pages side by side
@section Two pages side by side

@cindex two pages
@cindex spreads
@cindex book layout

@table @asis
@item @kbd{2} (@code{vellumory-cycle-spread})
@kindex 2
@findex vellumory-cycle-spread
Cycle between single pages@comma{} two pages
  as a printed book opens (the first page alone@comma{} then 2–3@comma{} 4–5)@comma{} and two
  pages in pairs (1–2@comma{} 3–4).
@end table

Scrolling stays continuous.  @code{n} and @code{p} move by a pair of pages@comma{} the header
line names both@comma{} and fitting the width or the page fills the window with
the pair.  @code{vellumory-spread} chooses the layout documents open with@comma{} and
@code{vellumory-spread-gap} the gap between the two pages.

If @code{vellumory-spread} is not set@comma{} documents that ask for two columns or two
pages open that way: with odd pages on the left in pairs@comma{} with odd pages
on the right as a book.

@node Page colours and dark themes
@section Page colours and dark themes

@cindex dark theme
@cindex page colours
@cindex night mode

Pages can be shown in four colourings:

@table @asis
@item original
the document's own colours;
@item theme colours
text in your Emacs theme's foreground colour on its
background;
@item inverted
dark pages with light text@comma{} the brightness inverted and the
hues kept@comma{} so a red figure stays red;
@item inverted with a dark theme
inverted while your Emacs theme is dark@comma{}
original while it is light.  This is the value @code{auto} of
@code{vellumory-theme}.
@end table

@table @asis
@item @kbd{C-c C-d} (@code{vellumory-cycle-theme})
@kindex C-c C-d
@findex vellumory-cycle-theme
Cycle the page colours of this
  document: original@comma{} theme colours@comma{} inverted.  With @code{C-u}@comma{} choose any of
  the four by name.  With a number@comma{} take that one: @code{C-u 0 C-c C-d} is the
  original@comma{} 1 the theme colours@comma{} 2 inverted@comma{} 3 inverted with a dark theme.
@item @kbd{M-x vellumory-set-theme}
@findex vellumory-set-theme
Choose the page colours of this document
  by name.
@item @kbd{M-x vellumory-theme-original}
@itemx @kbd{M-x vellumory-theme-tint}
@itemx @kbd{M-x vellumory-theme-invert}
@itemx @kbd{M-x vellumory-theme-auto}
@findex vellumory-theme-original
@findex vellumory-theme-tint
@findex vellumory-theme-invert
@findex vellumory-theme-auto
Choose one of the four directly@comma{} for
  binding to keys of your own.
@item @kbd{M-x vellumory-night-mode}
@findex vellumory-night-mode
Turn night mode on or off for this
  document: inverted pages@comma{} whatever @code{vellumory-theme} says.  Turned off@comma{} the
  pages take @code{vellumory-theme} again.  It is @code{N} in the command menu and @code{zd}
  with evil.
@end table

@findex vellumory-dispatch-colours
In the command menu@comma{} @code{C} opens a small menu of page colours
(@code{vellumory-dispatch-colours}): @code{c} cycles@comma{} @code{o}@comma{} @code{t}@comma{} @code{i} and @code{a} choose original@comma{}
theme colours@comma{} inverted and inverted with a dark theme@comma{} and @code{n} toggles
night mode; the menu stays open and shows the colours in effect.  The
right-click menu has the same choices as radio buttons.

The recolouring is done by the renderer@comma{} so text stays crisp@comma{} and the
page previews in the sidebar follow the pages.  Parts of a page not yet
rendered are filled with the colour the paper will have@comma{} so a dark page
never flashes white while it renders.  Search and selection highlights
are blended to stay visible on dark pages.  When you change your Emacs
theme@comma{} documents in theme colours@comma{} or inverted with a dark theme@comma{} are
drawn again to match.  Set @code{vellumory-theme} to start every document in the
colours you prefer.

@node Reading mode
@section Reading mode

@cindex reading mode
@cindex reflow
@cindex narrow windows
@findex vellumory-reflow-mode
@findex vellumory-reflow-mode-menu
@findex vellumory-dispatch-reflow
@findex vellumory-reflow-customize
@findex vellumory-reflow-set-colours

A page is made for paper.  In a narrow window@comma{} or when you simply want to
read@comma{} reading mode shows the document as text that flows to the window:
one column at a comfortable line length@comma{} in the size@comma{} font and colours
you choose@comma{} much as the reading modes of PDF apps on phones do.

@table @asis
@item @kbd{C-c C-r} (@code{vellumory-reflow})
@kindex C-c C-r
@findex vellumory-reflow
Read this document reflowed to the
  window; in reading mode@comma{} return to the pages.  It is @code{m} in the command
  menu and "Reading mode (reflowed)" in the right-click menu.
@end table

Reading mode is a view.  The document is not changed@comma{} and leaving it
with @code{q} shows the pages in the same window@comma{} at the place you reached.  The
place you reach is also the one Vellumory remembers for the document.  The
reflowed text lives in a buffer of its own@comma{} @samp{*Reflow: NAME*}@comma{} whose header
line names the page you are on.

@menu
* Where the text comes from::
* Keys in reading mode::
* Colours@comma{} size and line length: Colours size and line length. 
* Narrow windows::
* What reading mode cannot do::
@end menu

@node Where the text comes from
@subsection Where the text comes from

The worker builds each page's text anew.  When the PDF is tagged@comma{} it
follows the document's structure tree: paragraphs@comma{} headings@comma{} lists@comma{}
tables@comma{} code@comma{} notes and figures keep their kind.  When it is not@comma{} it reads
the page's layout: each block of text becomes a paragraph@comma{} much larger
type a heading@comma{} and monospaced blocks code.  The lines of a paragraph flow
together@comma{} with hyphens at line ends joined; code keeps its line breaks and
indentation.

Figures@comma{} formulas@comma{} images and drawings are shown as pictures cut from the
page@comma{} sized so that their lettering is as large as the text around them@comma{}
never wider than the text and never taller than most of the window.
Their text becomes the pictures' alternative text@comma{} which @code{I} shows
instead.  Running heads@comma{} page numbers and other text outside the content
are left out: in a tagged document@comma{} the parts its structure marks as not
belonging to the content; in an untagged one@comma{} single lines in the
margins.  @code{H} shows them.  The page number where each page begins is shown
small (@code{B} hides it).

Links work: one within the document goes to its page@comma{} here in reading
mode; one to the web opens with @code{browse-url}.  Pages are loaded as you
read@comma{} in either direction@comma{} and about fourteen pages around the one you
read are kept in the buffer.

@node Keys in reading mode
@subsection Keys in reading mode

@table @asis
@item @kbd{q} (@code{vellumory-reflow-quit})
@kindex q
@findex vellumory-reflow-quit
Back to the pages@comma{} at the place reached.
  @code{C-c C-r} does the same.
@item @kbd{@key{SPC}}
@itemx @kbd{@key{DEL}}
@kindex SPC
@kindex DEL
Scroll by a screen@comma{} as in any Emacs buffer.
@item @kbd{n} (@code{vellumory-reflow-next-page})
@kindex n
@findex vellumory-reflow-next-page
Go to the start of the next page.
@item @kbd{p} (@code{vellumory-reflow-previous-page})
@kindex p
@findex vellumory-reflow-previous-page
Go to the start of the previous
  page.
@item @kbd{g} (@code{vellumory-reflow-goto-page})
@itemx @kbd{M-g g}
@kindex g
@kindex M-g g
@findex vellumory-reflow-goto-page
Go to a page by its number.
@item @kbd{<} (@code{vellumory-reflow-first-page})
@kindex <
@findex vellumory-reflow-first-page
Go to the first page.
@item @kbd{>} (@code{vellumory-reflow-last-page})
@kindex >
@findex vellumory-reflow-last-page
Go to the last page.
@item @kbd{o} (@code{vellumory-reflow-outline})
@itemx @kbd{i}
@kindex o
@kindex i
@findex vellumory-reflow-outline
Go to a heading of the document's contents@comma{} with completion.
@item @kbd{+}
@itemx @kbd{=}
@kindex +
@kindex =
Larger text (@code{text-scale-increase}).
@item @kbd{-}
@kindex -
Smaller text (@code{text-scale-decrease}).
@item @kbd{0} (@code{vellumory-reflow-reset-size})
@kindex 0
@findex vellumory-reflow-reset-size
The normal text size again.
@item @kbd{@{} (@code{vellumory-reflow-narrower})
@kindex @{
@findex vellumory-reflow-narrower
Shorter lines@comma{} by five characters.
@item @kbd{@}} (@code{vellumory-reflow-wider})
@kindex @}
@findex vellumory-reflow-wider
Longer lines@comma{} by five characters.
@item @kbd{C} (@code{vellumory-reflow-cycle-colours})
@kindex C
@findex vellumory-reflow-cycle-colours
Cycle the colours (next
  section).
@item @kbd{I} (@code{vellumory-reflow-toggle-images})
@kindex I
@findex vellumory-reflow-toggle-images
Show figures as pictures@comma{} or as
  their text.
@item @kbd{H} (@code{vellumory-reflow-toggle-running-text})
