@node Searching text
@section Searching text

@cindex search
@cindex incremental search
@cindex case sensitivity
@findex vellumory-search-quit

@table @asis
@item @kbd{/} (@code{vellumory-search})
@itemx @kbd{C-s}
@kindex /
@kindex C-s
@findex vellumory-search
Find text.  Matches are shown as you type@comma{} starting from where
  you are reading@comma{} and highlighted on the pages.  With a prefix argument
  (@code{C-u /})@comma{} case matters; otherwise it does not.
@item @kbd{M-n} (@code{vellumory-search-next})
@kindex M-n
@findex vellumory-search-next
Go to the next match@comma{} wrapping round at
  the end of the document.
@item @kbd{M-p} (@code{vellumory-search-previous})
@kindex M-p
@findex vellumory-search-previous
Go to the previous match.
@item @kbd{M-s c} (@code{vellumory-search-clear})
@kindex M-s c
@findex vellumory-search-clear
Remove the highlights.
@end table

While you type the search@comma{} these keys work as in isearch:

@table @asis
@item @kbd{C-s} (@code{vellumory-search-minibuffer-next})
@kindex C-s
@findex vellumory-search-minibuffer-next
Next match.  With nothing
  typed yet@comma{} bring back the previous search.
@item @kbd{C-r} (@code{vellumory-search-minibuffer-previous})
@kindex C-r
@findex vellumory-search-minibuffer-previous
Previous match.
@item @kbd{M-r} (@code{vellumory-search-minibuffer-toggle-regexp})
@kindex M-r
@findex vellumory-search-minibuffer-toggle-regexp
Switch between
  plain text and an Emacs regular expression.
@item @kbd{@key{RET}}
@kindex RET
Keep the result and stay at the match.
@item @kbd{C-g}
@kindex C-g
Give up and return to where you started.
@end table

Search works on the document's text@comma{} with Unicode@comma{} and a match may run
across lines.  The current match has its own colour (the faces
@code{vellumory-highlight-match} and @code{vellumory-highlight-current}).  A scanned
document without a text layer has nothing to find: add one with text
recognition (@code{e o}@comma{} see @ref{Document edits}).  While a search is still
working through a long document@comma{} @code{C-g} in the reader stops it
(@code{vellumory-search-quit}).

@node Regular expressions
@section Regular expressions

@cindex regexp search

@table @asis
@item @kbd{C-M-s} (@code{vellumory-search-regexp})
@kindex C-M-s
@findex vellumory-search-regexp
Find matches of an Emacs regular
  expression@comma{} the same way.  With a prefix argument@comma{} case matters.
@end table

The expression is matched against the page's characters@comma{} with its lines
joined by newlines@comma{} so a match may span lines; each line it covers is
highlighted.

@node Listing every match
@section Listing every match

@cindex occur
@cindex all matches
@findex vellumory-occur-mode
@findex vellumory-occur-goto

@table @asis
@item @kbd{M-s o} (@code{vellumory-occur})
@kindex M-s o
@findex vellumory-occur
List every line of the document that
  matches a regular expression@comma{} by page@comma{} with some text around each match
  (@code{vellumory-occur-context}).
@item @kbd{C-u M-s o}
@kindex C-u M-s o
The same over every open document.
@end table

In the list@comma{} @code{RET} (@code{vellumory-occur-goto}) shows a match in the reader@comma{}
highlighted@comma{} and @code{n} and @code{p} move through the list@comma{} showing each match.  @code{M-g n} and @code{M-g p}
(@code{next-error} and @code{previous-error}) step through the matches from anywhere.
The document's text is extracted once per version and kept; on the
756-page ISO 32000 standard that took 1.6 seconds on the test machine.

@table @asis
@item @kbd{M-x vellumory-occur-documents}
@findex vellumory-occur-documents
List the matching lines of several
  documents@comma{} by document and page.  In Dired it takes the marked files
  (@code{; o}); elsewhere every open document.  Four documents are read at a
  time.  @code{RET} opens a match's document at the match.
@end table

@node Every line at your fingertips
@section Every line at your fingertips

@cindex consult
@cindex lines of text

@table @asis
@item @kbd{M-s l} (@code{vellumory-consult-line})
@kindex M-s l
@findex vellumory-consult-line
Choose any line of the document's
  text@comma{} labelled with its page@comma{} and go there with the line highlighted.
@end table

With the consult package@comma{} the pages follow your choice as you move through
the candidates@comma{} and @code{consult-line} itself is remapped to this command in
documents (in Doom@comma{} so is @code{SPC s s}).  Without consult it is an ordinary
completing read.  consult also gains a hidden source of open documents for
@code{consult-buffer}: type @code{d SPC} there to narrow to them.

