The report has these sections:

@table @asis
@item Document
format and version@comma{} number of pages@comma{} size@comma{} objects and
revisions; encryption and the permissions it denies; the standards the
document claims (PDF/A@comma{} PDF/UA and others@comma{} read from its XMP metadata);
whether it is tagged and has a structure tree; its language; whether it
is linearized; and whether MuPDF had to repair its structure.
@item Signatures
see @ref{Signatures}.
@item Metadata
title@comma{} author@comma{} subject@comma{} keywords@comma{} creator and producer;
creation and modification dates in readable form; whether there is XMP
metadata.
@item Content
fonts (how many are embedded@comma{} how many have Unicode maps)@comma{}
images@comma{} annotations (links@comma{} form widgets@comma{} markup)@comma{} forms (including XFA)@comma{}
JavaScript (never executed here)@comma{} transparency@comma{} output intents@comma{} and
navigation: the outline@comma{} page labels and how the document asks to open.
@item Attachments
every embedded file.  @code{RET} on one opens it; it is copied
to Vellumory's cache first.
@item Page
for the page in view@comma{} its boxes (media@comma{} crop@comma{} bleed@comma{} trim@comma{} art)
in points and millimetres@comma{} its rotation and user unit@comma{} and the fonts@comma{}
images and annotations it uses.
@end table

Problems@comma{} such as fonts that are not embedded@comma{} are highlighted.  Claims
are reported as claims; whether the document really meets a standard is
what validation tells you.

