@node Setting up evil
@section Setting up evil

@findex vellumory-evil-setup

@lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'evil
  (require 'vellumory-evil)
  (vellumory-evil-setup))
@end lisp

@code{vellumory-evil-setup} starts documents@comma{} the contents@comma{} the page previews and
reading mode in normal state@comma{} and presentations in Emacs state (a presentation takes
every key itself).  It hides evil's cursor over pages@comma{} keeps a mouse
selection from entering visual state@comma{} and rebinds the mouse in normal state
so that selecting text works.  evil-snipe is turned off in documents and
their sidebars@comma{} where @code{s}@comma{} @code{f} and @code{t} mean the sidebar@comma{} links and previews.
The Doom module does all of this for you.

