@node Sidebars and views under evil
@section Sidebars and views under evil

In the contents sidebar: @code{RET} or @code{go} follows a heading@comma{} @code{TAB} folds and
@code{<backtab>} cycles the whole outline@comma{} @code{j} and @code{k} move between headings@comma{} @code{s}
switches to the previews@comma{} and @code{q} or @code{o} closes it.  In the page previews:
@code{RET} visits a page@comma{} @code{j} and @code{k} move@comma{} @code{s} switches to the contents@comma{} and @code{q} or
@code{t} closes them.  Marking pages for export works as in plain Emacs: @code{m} marks
the page at point@comma{} @code{u} unmarks it@comma{} @code{U} clears every mark and @code{x} exports the
marked pages.

@kindex zr (evil reading mode)
@kindex gO (evil reading mode)
@kindex g? (evil reading mode)
In reading mode the motions are evil's own@comma{} since it is text: @code{j}@comma{} @code{k}@comma{} @code{C-f}@comma{}
@code{C-b}@comma{} @code{gg}@comma{} @code{G} and the rest move through it as through any buffer.  On top of
them: @code{q} or @code{zr} returns to the pages@comma{} @code{]]} and @code{[[} go to the next and previous
page@comma{} @code{gO} to a heading of the contents@comma{} @code{+} and @code{-} change the text size and @code{=}
resets it@comma{} @code{C} cycles the colours@comma{} @code{TAB} and @code{<backtab>} move between links@comma{} and
@code{?} or @code{g?} opens reading mode's menu.

The keyboard caret's keys (see @ref{With the keyboard caret}) take precedence
over normal state while the caret is active.  In Vellumory's other buffers@comma{}
such as the history tree@comma{} the validation report@comma{} the comparison@comma{} the
details@comma{} the occur list@comma{} the syntax view@comma{} the batch table and the
annotation list@comma{} each buffer's own keys take precedence over normal
state.  So @code{c} in the history tree makes a state current rather than
starting evil's change operator.  In the syntax view@comma{} @code{q} closes the view
while it is read-only.

@node The Doom module
@section The Doom module

@cindex Doom Emacs
@cindex localleader

Doom's @samp{:tools vellumory} module (see @ref{Doom Emacs} for installing it) sets
up:

@itemize
@item
lazy loading: only the small file associations load at startup@comma{} and the
reader loads with the first document;
@item
evil@comma{} when @samp{:editor evil} is enabled;
@item
a doom-modeline segment with the page@comma{} the zoom@comma{} the search status and
the caret@comma{} instead of the header line;
@item
a popup rule that shows page text on the right;
@item
document buffers as "real" buffers@comma{} so they join workspaces and appear in
@code{switch-to-buffer} (the sidebars do not);
@item
@code{ESC} clearing search highlights first@comma{} then the selection;
@item
localleader keys with which-key descriptions@comma{} listed below;
@item
with @samp{:lang latex}@comma{} Vellumory as AUC@TeX{}'s viewer@comma{} so @code{SPC m v} in a @TeX{}
buffer shows the line at point;
@item
in Org@comma{} @code{SPC n l} (@code{org-store-link}) stores the exact place in a document.
@end itemize

