The localleader prefixes @code{e} (edit)@comma{} @code{a} (annotate) and @code{x} (export) hold the
same commands as the plain Emacs keys: @code{e r} rotates@comma{} @code{e u} undoes@comma{} @code{a h}
highlights@comma{} @code{x x} extracts pages@comma{} @code{x s} splits and @code{x t} exports the text.

In Dired@comma{} the localleader prefix @code{v} acts on the marked documents: @code{v v}
validates@comma{} @code{v e} edits each@comma{} @code{v i} summarizes and @code{v m} merges.  The @code{;} keys of
plain Emacs work as well.

