@node Customization
@chapter Customization

@cindex customization
@cindex options

Every option can be set with Customize (@code{M-x customize-group RET vellumory}@comma{}
or @code{@comma{}} in the command menu) or with @code{setq} in your init file.  The defaults
are chosen to work well without any configuration.  The group @code{vellumory}
holds general options and the subgroups @code{vellumory-reader}@comma{}
@code{vellumory-reflow}@comma{} @code{vellumory-thumbnails}@comma{} @code{vellumory-select}@comma{}
@code{vellumory-annotate}@comma{} @code{vellumory-present}@comma{} @code{vellumory-sync} and
@code{vellumory-syntax}.

A small example:

@lisp
(setq vellumory-spread 'book            ; two pages@comma{} as a book opens
      vellumory-theme 'tint             ; pages in the theme's colours
      vellumory-show-thumbnails nil     ; no page previews at first
      vellumory-confirm-external-links nil)
@end lisp

