@node Rendering
@section Rendering

These options tune the renderer.  The defaults come from measurements (see
@ref{Performance and how it is measured}); change them only if you have a
reason.

@defopt vellumory-strip-height
Height in logical pixels of the
  image strips pages are made of.  Taller strips make scrolling cheaper@comma{}
  because redisplay costs about a millisecond per line of images in view.
  On the ISO 32000 standard@comma{} 192-pixel strips gave a mean scroll step of
  2.9 ms and a worst of 21–27 ms; 768-pixel strips 1.7 ms and under 5 ms@comma{}
  without rendering more pixels.  Default: @code{768}.
@end defopt

@defopt vellumory-tile-width
Width of a tile when pages are wider
  than the window@comma{} so that only the visible columns are rendered.  Default:
  @code{640}.
@end defopt

@defopt vellumory-refine-delay
Seconds without motion before
  previews are replaced by sharp tiles.  Default: @code{0.09}.
@end defopt

@defopt vellumory-immediate-budget
Render sharp tiles at once@comma{} even
  while moving@comma{} if the worker's measured cost for this document says they
  take less than this many milliseconds.  Default: @code{14}.
@end defopt

@defopt vellumory-preview-scale
Resolution of the whole-page
  previews shown while moving@comma{} relative to sharp tiles.  Default: @code{0.25}.
@end defopt

@defopt vellumory-prefetch-screens
Screens rendered ahead of and
  behind the direction of motion when Emacs is idle.  Default: @code{(1.0 . 0.5)}.
@end defopt

@defopt vellumory-retain-screens
Decoded images within this many
  screens of a window are kept; those further away are released.  Default:
  @code{2.0}.
@end defopt

@defopt vellumory-gc-threshold
The garbage collection threshold
  while reading moves and while pages are laid out; garbage is collected
  once reading rests.  Default: @code{67108864} (64 MiB).
@end defopt

@defopt vellumory-gc-idle-delay
Seconds reading must rest before
  the garbage it left is collected@comma{} so that collections do not fall into a
  scroll step.  @code{nil} lets Emacs collect as usual.  When @code{gcmh-mode} is on (as
  in Doom)@comma{} Vellumory leaves collection to it.  Default: @code{0.5}.
